\section{Reproducibility}
\label{app:repro}

\paragraph{Data and code.}
The score matrices are the 13 files released with~\citep{zhang2025miss} under the MIT licence, at commit \texttt{55faff49}; only the data files and the model lists are used.
The code, the instructions with environment, seeds, commands and run times, the result tables behind every figure and table, and the map from each script to the figure or table it produces are in the \texttt{code/} directory delivered with this paper.

\paragraph{Compute.}
Everything ran on CPUs. The 38 main jobs (one per benchmark and split) took $3.3$ CPU-hours, of which interpolation took $1.4$, lineage $1.2$ and extrapolation $0.7$ (from under one minute to $22$ minutes per job, the longest for MMLU-Pro); the sensitivity splits took $1.4$ CPU-hours more, $4.7$ CPU-hours in all.
All random draws derive from one base seed and the tuple (benchmark, split, fold, $n$, draw, design).

